{"id": "EUVD-2026-103963", "enisaUuid": "661c5b2a-af47-3e62-a725-9f213d71dc3e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: count only matching reservations in reserved switch\n\nieee80211_vif_use_reserved_switch() validates a replacement by counting\nassigned links on ctx->replace_ctx and treating reservations too\nbroadly. A link can still be assigned to the old channel context while\nholding a reservation that belongs to a different replacement\noperation.\n\nThat can make the current replacement appear complete too early. If\nanother link finalizes first, the function can free the\nWILL_BE_REPLACED chanctx while the unmatched link and driver still use\nit, leading to a use-after-free in later beacon generation.\n\nRequire an in-place reservation to point at the current replacement\ncontext, and require the reserved and assigned contexts to be the\nmatching replacement pair, before counting or moving the link.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ae6ed5b6074df5f3da05fd74c40bb24c5c9b41d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d31f655e44631891788ca67018ec5e1ed1c7de86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03525b632908b049f4d04cc8a71cdff2329589cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cc54a000960bc88f8c58940164dca0e601ab39c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/437f3727b4fd715266c296435c116288f82666fd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98709", "GHSA-g34c-vjm7-4vq5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38473e73-3f0a-35dc-af7b-3a2fea27dc2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "442e3609-66aa-34f8-8adf-4c746c8014a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bcae31d9cb1ebfad3ad5a3eea04c8cdc329a04f <d31f655e44631891788ca67018ec5e1ed1c7de86"}, {"id": "472ceb20-09fb-39d7-bde2-f919b1aa0e5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "5637a9e3-366a-3c04-b256-ee5f9f19b0d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6eb9972a-9a58-3dbf-af62-5a73be06eedc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7674e522-ea12-3125-b9bd-6bc4192b0cfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bcae31d9cb1ebfad3ad5a3eea04c8cdc329a04f <437f3727b4fd715266c296435c116288f82666fd"}, {"id": "8da3abe4-f5da-37fd-a776-89d8e55580e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bcae31d9cb1ebfad3ad5a3eea04c8cdc329a04f <4ae6ed5b6074df5f3da05fd74c40bb24c5c9b41d"}, {"id": "95772867-d1d5-38d7-97a8-eed9552927b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bcae31d9cb1ebfad3ad5a3eea04c8cdc329a04f <5cc54a000960bc88f8c58940164dca0e601ab39c"}, {"id": "b1c1e78d-f6ce-3f2f-b7fc-9b6346dd08e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "bec80bfa-d90f-3acd-80e9-bb2e2d1bd752", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "c68be127-da1e-3916-9107-3dd4f7fb9163", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.17"}, {"id": "eb1791ea-fb74-37d3-a694-abce63293ecc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bcae31d9cb1ebfad3ad5a3eea04c8cdc329a04f <03525b632908b049f4d04cc8a71cdff2329589cf"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f6ea4ce7-4c03-320c-babe-3c74f5216bee", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}